# The Quiet Archive - EP10 A Medieval Castle After Dark (a November night in an English castle, late 1400s)
# Structure: a journey INWARD, ring by ring - from the road outside, through the gate and the outer courtyard, into the
#   great hall, up onto the walls, and finally into the innermost chamber (first time the channel moves "outside -> in").
#   The household watchman ("wayte") who pipes the watch four times on winter nights is the thread through the night.
# New scenes: "castle" = the castle from across the moat at dusk: curtain wall with round towers and crenellations, a
#   twin-towered gatehouse with a lit arch and a torch, the old square keep behind, banners stirring on the towers
#   (_banners), the moat holding the reflections of lit windows (_wlights); a willow and reeds on the near bank.
# "bailey" = the outer courtyard seen from inside the gate: the lowered portcullis with its iron grid, lean-to stables
#   with a horse's head over the half-door, the stone well-head with its windlass and bucket, the bakehouse with the oven
#   mouth breathing a red glow (_oven) and smoke from its chimney, a dovecote, the watchman crossing slowly with his
#   lantern (_walker).
# "hall" = the great hall: timber roof trusses with arched braces, a smoke louvre, the central hearth (fires), the dais
#   with the high table and a painted cloth behind it, trestle boards stacked against the wall, sleepers on straw pallets,
#   a hound curled by the fire, the screens with two doorways; the rising smoke drifts up into the louvre (smoke).
# "wallwalk" = on top of the curtain wall: battlements in one-point perspective, a brazier glowing in a turret corner,
#   the countryside below with a village, a church tower and a river under the moon, and a cloaked watchman pacing
#   slowly along the walk and back (_sentry).
# "solar" = the lady's chamber: a great bed with a canopy (tester) and curtains, a fur coverlet, a window seat with
#   stone benches in a deep embrasure and a two-light window with moonlight, a candle in a wall niche, a chest, a little
#   dog asleep, a hanging cloth that sways very slightly in the draught (_hanging).
# New "thistledown" particles (soft seed tufts drifting sideways outside); palette keys "stone" and "banner".
KICKER = "Calm History for Sleep"
TITLE = "A Medieval Castle After Dark"
TAIL_SCENE = "castle"
